PREAMBLE

This license makes the Software (all code, probes, tools, documentation,
schemas, examples and assets in this repository) available in two ways:

  (a) EDUCATIONAL & RESEARCH USE — 100% free, no royalty, for everyone; and
  (b) ANY OTHER USE (including any commercial, business, for-profit or
      production/"real-time" deployment) — only under a separate written
      Commercial License from the Copyright Holder, carrying a royalty of
      five percent (5%) of Net Revenue of the project that uses the Software.

This is a source-available license. It is NOT an OSI-approved open-source
license: the rights granted here are limited to Educational & Research Use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means the contents of this repository — source code, scripts,
    probes, schemas, documentation, examples, assets and any modified or
    derived versions of them.

1.2 "Educational & Research Use" means use that is not primarily intended for
    or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation,
    including: use by students, teachers and schools; academic and
    non-profit research; personal study and self-education; evaluation,
    benchmarking and experimentation that does not operate as part of a
    revenue-generating product or service; and journalism or public
    commentary about the Software.

1.3 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software as a component of, or in
    the operation of, a product, service, system or activity from which
    revenue is derived or is intended to be derived — including but not
    limited to: deployment in a commercial product or paid service;
    incorporation into client deliverables for a fee; use by a company,
    firm or individual in their ordinary business operations; or use that
    offers any commercial advantage. Any Commercial Use requires a
    Commercial License under Section 3.

1.4 "Net Revenue" means the gross revenue of the project attributable to the
    product or service in which the Software is used, minus only: (i) taxes
    collected on behalf of third parties (e.g. GST/VAT), and (ii) fees paid
    directly to payment processors for the relevant transactions. Revenue is
    not reduced by other costs, expenses or third-party components.

1.5 "Contribution" means any work intentionally submitted to the Copyright
    Holder for inclusion in the Software.

